This is a faceless cinematic journey in a fixed five-beat format (POV sprint + body-slam through the door in one continuous motion, POV brisk walk across the first room to the top of a straight staircase going down, OFF-POV from across the lower room showing the descent (person coming DOWN), OFF-POV lateral tracking across the lower room, OFF-POV follow into another luxurious room). Honor the camera mode of this scene: scenes 1-2 are first-person POV (raw body-cam/GoPro/handheld footage at chest/eye level, slightly imperfect framing, body never visible except S1 arms swinging in the lower frame and the body-slam impact at end-of-S1); scenes 3-5 are calm off-POV third-person in which the traveler is seen only from behind or in profile, face never shown, clothing locked across S3, S4, S5. The descent is always a normal short straight step staircase going down, structurally attached, in an enclosed stairwell with no outdoor window, with any handrail on the side wall only. In K3 the visible stairs clearly read as the person descending, NEVER ascending. Keep the locked structure identity through the exterior portions. The image must advance the journey only a believable short step from the previous keyframe. No on-screen text, numbers, logos, or watermarks. Single continuous frame only.

motion.prompt_template:
{kling_prompt}

This is a faceless cinematic journey in a fixed five-beat format toward and into a hidden luxurious secret living space. Honor the camera mode stated for this scene. SCENES 1-2 FIRST-PERSON POV (body-cam/GoPro/handheld). Scene 1: the camera is a BODY-CAM on a PANICKED sprinting runner FLEEING on a non-linear weaving path — EXTREME footstep bob (camera jolts DOWN-UP AND side-to-side with each footfall, 3–4 strides per second flat-out sprint, frame rotates 8–15 degrees per stride, motion blur at frame edges), WORLD RUSHES PAST at sprint speed (~6–7 m/s — ground flying past beneath, terrain blurring at edges), per-stride SURGE-AND-SETTLE (camera lurches forward as foot pushes off, jolts down hard as foot lands), panicked panting breath, head turning to occasionally scan and glance over the shoulder backwards (camera NOT always pointed at the destination door — the door enters and exits the frame), arms/hands swinging in and out of the bottom of the frame, AND at the end of the clip the runner BODY-SLAMS the door (body, not hand, makes contact), the door YIELDS INWARD instantly (swings AWAY from the camera INTO the structure), and the runner BARGES THROUGH without slowing or pausing — clip ends inside the first room mid-stride. Scene 2: a hurried purposeful POV walk across the modest first room interior to the top of the descending staircase, reduced bob, still handheld, ending at the top looking DOWN. SCENES 3-5 OFF-POV THIRD-PERSON: calm controlled motion. Scene 3: the FIRST off-POV beat — a wide view across the lower room with the structurally-attached straight step staircase visible on one side of the frame and the lone traveler visibly DESCENDING those stairs (coming DOWN from upstairs, never ascending). Scene 4: a slow horizontal lateral tracking shot across the lower room while the traveler walks calmly in ONE consistent forward direction; interior locked, person appearance locked. Scene 5: a smooth continuous follow from behind as the traveler walks through into another luxurious room with same materials/palette; person appearance IDENTICAL to S4.

Keep the locked structure identity through the exterior portions. Advance the journey only a believable short distance per clip. The descent is always a normal short straight step staircase going DOWN, structurally attached — never a ladder, never floating, never climbing up. The K3 stairs MUST read as the person descending, never ascending. The stairwell is fully enclosed with no outdoor window. Any handrail is on the side wall only. The audio is natural diegetic sound only that matches the action exactly — wind/sea/rain plus HARD pounding footsteps on the SPECIFIC ground surface and panicked panting breath (S1, plus a body-slam thud and door creak at end), brisk footsteps on the SPECIFIC first-room floor material (S2), footsteps descending the SPECIFIC staircase material (S3), calm walking footsteps on the SPECIFIC lower-room floor material (S4-S5) — absolutely NO music or score. Every clip must depict ONE continuous motion from start to end — no time jumps, no mid-clip cuts, no skipping, no pauses; in S3, S4, S5 the person walks in ONE consistent direction without turning, reversing, walking backwards, melting, or changing appearance.
